 03 Jun 2020:"}, {"text": "I’ll cover fiscal theory and the recent inflation (again!) of course, but also more recent thoughts on the great puzzle of monetary economics, how central banks can lower inflation by raising nominal interest rates.", "reference": "2025 September 30, John H. Cochrane, “Brunner lecture”, in The Grumpy Economist, archived from the original on 14 Jan 2026:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(qualifying nouns of family relationship) Involving more generations than the qualified word implies — as many extra generations as repetitions of the word great (from 1510s). [see Derived terms]", "tags": [], "examples": ["great-grandfather, great-great-grandfather, great-great-great-grandfather"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "as", "name": "Assamese"}, "word": "আজো"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "iso-"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete, postpositive, followed by 'with') Pregnant; large with young; full of.", "tags": ["obsolete", "postpositional"], "examples": ["great with child", "great with hope"], "quotes": [{"text": "the ewes great with young", "reference": "1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, Psalms 78:71:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(obsolete, except with 'friend' and similar words such as 'mate', 'buddy') Intimate; familiar.", "tags": ["obsolete"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "those that are so great with him", "reference": "1625, Francis [Bacon], “Of Followers and Friends”, in The Essayes […], 3rd edition, London: […] Iohn Haviland for Hanna Barret, →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(applied to actions, thoughts and feelings) Arising from or possessing idealism; admirable; commanding; illustrious; eminent.", "tags": [